From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:18:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Trim the menus for a handheld console

No Read This!, which explains the keyboard, no Change View, the view
always fills the top screen, and no Control: the buttons are the
joystick, without mouse or keyboard, and customizing them captured the
B button that leaves the screen. Sound moves down above Quit, like the
options in other games. The DS always plays the AdLib and digitized
sounds, so its sound effects, digitized sounds and music are just
Disabled or Enabled, older configs with the PC speaker or Sound Source
get Enabled. The settings are kept in the config as soon as it is left,
a handheld is often just switched off. In a game the menu
has no Quit, End Game leaves it. New Game is the first item selected,
ReadConfig no longer reactivates the item that was Read This! by its
index. Back (B or START) leaves the main menu like Back to Game/Demo
instead of asking to quit, Quit still asks.

The episodes the shareware lacks say where the data of the full game
goes instead of pointing to Read This!.
